   "file": "plugins/specclaw/hooks/refresh.ts",
   "fp": "136d35741b22",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 14,
   "message": "`refresh()` calls `$.ui.status(statusText(latest))` without awaiting it. If `ui.status` rejects asynchronously, the rejection escapes `refreshQuietly`'s catch and the gate's `.catch` as an unhandled promise rejection. The status line silently keeps its old text, and nothing reports that the status could not be set. Await the call, as `refreshQuietly` already does.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B3",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/hooks/place.ts",
   "fp": "f7d82ead4924",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 5,
   "message": "`BAD_NAME` (`[. ]$`, `..`) is applied to every unresolved name, including ones outside the project. `placePath` then returns `undefined`, and `gateDecision` holds any `target === undefined` path. So a new file outside the project is warned about or denied: one whose name ends in a dot or space, or one under a missing folder reached through `..`. Return the lexically joined path when the resolved ancestor is outside the root, or apply the unplaceable rule only to names under the root.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B6",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw/hooks/register.tsx",
   "fp": "f35adccf9fa3",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 13,
   "message": "An unknown `gate` value is reported only in the `session.start` handler. If the mod is loaded or reloaded after session start, the gate runs as `warn` with no toast naming the bad value. Report the unknown value from the gate handler as well, once per session.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
